## Critical rule for the native KB folder

<!-- WHEN native-kb -->
`<NativeKbPath>` is off-limits for agent writes.

Agents must not create, edit, move, rename, or delete files in that folder.
Reading is allowed only when an explicit operational flow genuinely requires it
(for example, the read-only identity resolution done by
`Resolve-<KbName>KbIdentity.ps1`).
<!-- END WHEN -->
<!-- WHEN xpz-only -->
No native KB folder is recorded for this XPZ-only workspace. If one is added
later, record it in the Identification section and in
`scripts/Resolve-<KbName>KbIdentity.ps1`; it is then off-limits for agent
writes, and agents read it only when an explicit operational flow genuinely
requires it.
<!-- END WHEN -->

## Functional structure of the KB workspace

- `scripts`: thin local wrappers that delegate to the shared engine.
- `Temp`: temporary files and disposable reports.
- `IdeXpzExports`: inbox for `.xpz` files exported from the GeneXus IDE.
- `KbObjectsXml`: official materialized snapshot; read-only for agents
  outside the official sync flow.
- `KbIntelligence`: derived, regenerable index.

## Operational state

The operational state of this workspace and the materialization/index
timestamps are not recorded in this section. A declarative mirror of a
timestamp silently goes stale because nothing keeps it consistent with the
authoritative source. To learn the current state, use:

- `suggested_operational_state` and the other audit dimensions: output of
  `Test-<KbName>KbSetupAudit.ps1` (run it on every audit).
- `last_xpz_materialization_run_at`: frontmatter of `kb-source-metadata.md`,
  maintained by the **sync** workflow.
- `last_index_build_run_at`: `metadata` table of the SQLite index at
  `KbIntelligence\kb-intelligence.sqlite`, exposed by
  `Query-<KbName>KbIntelligence.ps1 -Query index-metadata`.
- Operational index freshness gate:
  `Test-<KbName>KbIndexGate.ps1` - returns `GATE_OK` or `BLOCK: <reason>`.

Do not record literal timestamps (`last_xpz_materialization_run_at`,
`last_index_build_run_at`) in this section, in other sections of this
`AGENTS.md`, or in the local `README.md`.

## Local wrappers

The wrappers in `scripts` use the shared Mimir Lite checkout:

```text
<MimirLiteRoot>
```

Expected wrappers:

- `Test-<KbName>KbPowerShellRuntime.ps1`: first gate of any operational use;
  requires `pwsh` 7.4 or later on Windows (7.4.6 or later on Linux and macOS)
  and returns `POWERSHELL_RUNTIME_OK` or `BLOCK: ...`.
- `Test-<KbName>KbSetupFreshness.ps1`: precondition of the global trigger;
  compares the audited contract signature (`setup_contract_signature_*`) with
  the current signature of the **setup** workflow and returns `GATE_ONLY` or
  `AUDIT_REQUIRED: <reason>`.
- `Set-<KbName>KbSetupAuditTimestamp.ps1`: writes `last_setup_audit_run_at` and
  `setup_contract_signature_*` into `kb-source-metadata.md` after a successful
  setup audit; use it in the same session when the freshness check returned
  `AUDIT_REQUIRED` for a missing, absent, or stale signature and the full audit
  plus the gate passed.
- `Update-<KbName>KbFromXpz.ps1`: materializes XPZ/XML into `KbObjectsXml`,
  surgically updates the materialization fields of `kb-source-metadata.md`
  (engine `Sync-GeneXusXpzToXml.ps1`), preserving `last_setup_audit_run_at` and
  `setup_contract_signature_*`, and calls the index refresh unless running in
  `VerifyOnly` mode. It runs the session reminder and the `-FailOnUnknownTypes`
  pre-scan before materializing (see the XPZ catalog section below).
- `Test-<KbName>KbFullSnapshot.ps1`: full check in verify-only mode.
- `Rebuild-<KbName>KbIntelligenceIndex.ps1`: regenerates and validates
  `KbIntelligence\kb-intelligence.sqlite`.
- `Query-<KbName>KbIntelligence.ps1`: queries the derived index, including
  `index-metadata`.
- `Test-<KbName>KbIndexGate.ps1`: freshness gate - checks structure, SQLite, and
  timestamps and returns `GATE_OK` or throws `BLOCK: <reason>`; it must be the
  single execution point of the gate.
- `Get-<KbName>KbMetadata.ps1`: reads key fields of `kb-source-metadata.md`
  without inline regex in callers; exposes at least
  `last_xpz_materialization_run_at`, `kb_name`, and `source_guid`.
- `Resolve-<KbName>KbIdentity.ps1`: reconciles the stable identity of the local
  native KB when the exported XPZ came with an empty or incomplete `Source`;
  delegates to the shared engine `Resolve-GeneXusKbIdentity.ps1` in read-only
  mode and, when called with the explicit update option, to
  `Update-MimirKbSourceMetadataIdentity.ps1`. With no native KB folder recorded
  (an XPZ-only workspace), it reports `NATIVE_KB_NOT_RECORDED`, exits `3`, and
  changes nothing.
- `Test-<KbName>KbMetadataWrapper.ps1`: validates the functional contract of
  `Get-<KbName>KbMetadata.ps1` against `kb-source-metadata.md`; returns
  `METADATA_WRAPPER_OK`, `PENDING_DATA`, or `BLOCK: ...`.
- `Test-<KbName>KbObjectsXmlNaming.ps1`: read-only audit of the directory
  naming of `KbObjectsXml` against the object type found in each XML;
  returns `NAMING_OK`, `NAMING_DIVERGENT`, or `NAMING_INDETERMINATE`.
- `Test-<KbName>KbStructure.ps1`: report of the presence or absence of expected
  folders, scripts, and artifacts; returns `STRUCTURE_OK` or lists the missing
  components.
- `Test-<KbName>KbSetupAudit.ps1`: aggregated setup audit; consolidates the
  deterministic evidence of the gates above into one output.

Engine scripts whose parameters are fully dynamic on every run do not need a
local wrapper; call them directly by the absolute path of the shared checkout.

## XPZ catalog (unknown types and local override)

- Effective catalog = `skills/mimir-lite/scripts/gx-object-type-catalog.json` in
  the shared checkout + `scripts/gx-object-type-catalog.override.json` in this
  workspace when it exists.
- A local override is a stopgap (`upstreamPending` declared); it is never
  silent. The reminder classifies entries as pending, redundant, or divergent.
  `CLEANUP_RECOMMENDED` must enter the consolidated plan as an explicit,
  approved offer of local cleanup (for example, removing only the redundant
  entry), even when the plan also carries a mandatory signature re-stamp; it
  does not authorize automatic removal.
- In each new session, when `scripts/gx-object-type-catalog.override.json`
  exists, run `Test-MimirCatalogOverrideSessionReminder.ps1` from the shared
  checkout with `-KbWorkspaceRoot` pointing at this workspace (an optional thin
  local wrapper) before a long sync or materialization. With no override file
  there is nothing to remind. If `noticeRequired=true`, warn the user according
  to `status`: upstream pending, blocked or invalid override, or recommended
  local cleanup.
- Before materializing a full XPZ or a first load, the pre-scan is mandatory:
  `Get-GeneXusXpzObjectInventory.ps1` with `-FailOnUnknownTypes` and
  `-KbWorkspaceRoot`. If it blocks, do not call sync until the type is resolved.
- An unknown type in the package is a catalog gap, not a defect of the KB's XPZ.
  Ask the user whether consulting an external GeneXus modeling tool and the
  official GeneXus wiki/docs is authorized before registering an override or
  requesting an upstream update.
- Register a local override only with explicit consent, through
  `Register-GeneXusObjectTypeCatalogOverride.ps1` (`-UserApproved`). JSON
  template: `examples/gx-object-type-catalog.override.json.example`.
- Copyable prompt for the maintainer of the shared base:
  `New-GeneXusUnknownTypeMaintainerPrompt.ps1`.

## Index triage

For any question about existence, location, technical impact, dependents,
dependencies, or short functional investigation of objects in this KB, use the
Mimir Lite **find** workflow. The gate is the only entry point to the index:

1. Check that `scripts/Test-<KbName>KbIndexGate.ps1` exists.
   - If missing: end the query and offer an update through the **setup**
     workflow.
2. Run the gate:
   ```text
   pwsh -NoProfile -File "<WorkspaceRoot>/scripts/Test-<KbName>KbIndexGate.ps1"
   ```
   - `GATE_OK` -> proceed with the **find** workflow.
   - `BLOCK: <reason>` -> end the query and offer an index rebuild.
3. Never access `KbIntelligence\kb-intelligence.sqlite` directly by any tool -
   Python, sqlite3, inline PowerShell, Bash, or any other means.
4. Never compensate for a blocked gate with a manual read of SQLite, validation
   JSON, an isolated `kb-source-metadata.md`, file dates, or official XML.
5. `KbObjectsXml` is the normative source; consult it only after the gate is
   released and only for the minimum set the triage points to.

## GeneXus/XPZ rules

- For GeneXus modeling, analysis, or structure questions, an external GeneXus
  tool (for example `nexa`) may be used when the user has one; anything covered
  by a Mimir Lite workflow follows that workflow instead.
- For XPZ files, exported KB XML, or syncing an XPZ, use the Mimir Lite **sync**
  workflow. The supported input is an XPZ exported by the user from the GeneXus
  IDE.
- This workspace is read-side only: do not generate, clone, package, build, or
  import GeneXus objects from here.
- `KbObjectsXml` is the official materialized snapshot; `KbIntelligence` is
  only a derived, regenerable layer.
- `last_xpz_materialization_run_at` must exist in `kb-source-metadata.md`.
- `last_index_build_run_at`, in SQLite, must be equal to or later than
  `last_xpz_materialization_run_at` before broad triage.
